(* merkle.test.mligo — validate the REAL Merkle frontier against the Rust golden
   vector (tezos/rollup-kernel/tests/merkle_golden_throwaway.rs, the throwaway
   harness driving core::hash_merkle + the kernel append_note walk).

   Golden vector (DEPTH=48, cm = [0x..01, 0x..02, 0x..03]):
     EMPTY_TREE_ROOT (zero_hashes[48])
       = 0xe8b9679e792c563f2c2be996e164aba5be471480fd46e63cfacd855d87dccf02
     FINAL_ROOT (after appending the 3 commitments)
       = 0xf1c88c5d2b04434a792962ad6ad8f949a9640bc924526248c33e3c013d80d200

   BLAKE2S(mrklSP__) is the stubbed Layer-1 primitive: blake_mrkl below carries
   the exact (a‖b -> digest) pairs of the reference (251-bit-truncated digests).
   What is VALIDATED here is the SURROUNDING frontier algorithm: the even/odd
   slot management, the zero-hash mixing, the per-level index walk, and the
   zero_hashes recurrence — none of which is stubbed.

   Run:  ligo run test merkle.test.mligo *)

